WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:07.889
This video went viral recently after

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:09.299
it was uploaded to Twitter by a

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.159
pro-labor advocacy group called

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.079
More Perfect Union, which then

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:14.639
pointed the finger at the National

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:16.769
Restaurant Association, a lobby

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:18.389
group funded by big food

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:20.219
corporations, calling it a

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:22.139
key driver behind new bills,

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:24.479
letting kids work dangerous jobs.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.519
Sure, taking drive thru orders

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:27.899
and slinging waffle fries at a

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:29.669
Chick-fil-A your dad owns sounds

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:30.725
like the definition of danger

00:00:30.726 --> 00:00:32.849
exactly like working

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:33.759
in a coal mine.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:35.279
Over the past year to help deal with

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:36.059
labor shortages.

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:37.289
Several states have pushed for

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:38.819
legislative changes that would let

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:40.139
more teenagers work.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.879
New Jersey enacted a bill allowing

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.829
16 year olds to work up to 50

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:45.389
hours a week during summer break

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:47.189
with parental approval.

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:48.749
In Ohio, the legislature is

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:50.519
considering a proposal that would

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:52.409
make it possible for 14 and 15

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:53.939
year olds to work longer hours

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:55.259
during the school year.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:56.699
And it's one of the few policies

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:58.169
Democrats and Republicans in the

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:00.119
state legislature agree on.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.129
Last month, Arkansas Governor Sarah

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:03.929
Huckabee Sanders signed a bill that

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.939
eliminated a requirement that 14

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:08.099
and 15 year olds obtain a permit

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:09.149
before getting a job.

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:11.489
These bills don't primarily benefit

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:13.319
the big food lobby, as the

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.329
union backed group that posted video

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:17.219
claims. And it's not an evil plot

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.469
to exploit children for profit.

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:21.359
The people who stand to benefit most

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:23.699
are actually teenagers themselves,

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:25.169
who, by having a job, can learn to

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:26.729
show up on time, follow

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:29.069
instructions, work collaboratively

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:30.789
and manage money that they earned

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.619
themselves, and therefore value

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:34.529
it more. "I feel as if I've learned

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:36.239
so much from this simple job over

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:38.309
the past few years," one teen

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:40.019
who worked as a ski instructor wrote

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:42.089
to the New York Times for a 2022

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:43.739
piece about the reality of holding a

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:45.419
part time job while going to school.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:46.619
"I've learned how to work with

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:46.650
children, become a better teacher,
and how to help different people
based

00:01:46.651 --> 00:01:47.651
on how they learn new skills." "My

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:54.299
job has helped me personally in many

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.189
ways. I was super shy before

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:57.509
I started and now I am more

00:01:57.510 --> 00:01:59.009
confident,"  added another high

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:00.719
school student who is working five

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:01.949
days a week after school.

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:03.689
"I learned time management so that I

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.459
can get from school to work and then

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:07.439
come home and do homework." There's

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:08.939
plenty of data that backs up the

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:10.739
claim that holding a job as a teen

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:11.789
has positive effects.

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:13.619
A 2016 paper published in the

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:14.969
Southern Economic Journal, for

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:16.499
example, found that high schoolers

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:17.999
working 20 hours a week during their

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.009
senior year had 12%

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:21.689
higher earnings in their careers

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:22.589
than those that didn't.

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:23.999
Although that wage premium has

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.229
declined over the years for

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:26.399
complicated reasons.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:27.959
In a job, teens are forced to

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:29.519
discover or build out parts of

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:31.229
themselves that are not required for

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:33.899
school, home or sports, psychologist

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.399
Lisa Damour told The Washington Post

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:37.049
last year. She also stressed that

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:38.819
having a job teaches kids to answer

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:40.479
to adults who aren't their parents

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:41.819
because when they do the same thing

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:43.409
over and over, there's no need to

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:45.269
grow. We need to stop treating

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:47.549
teenagers as inherently fragile

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:48.719
or they'll become that way.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:50.999
Real world exposure to the challenge

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.619
of getting paid to do things that

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:54.539
other people value will benefit

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:56.159
them for the rest of their lives.

